! Candidate console-managed baseline for the site-to-site VPN router.
! Select <SECRET-TYPE> as 8 (PBKDF2-SHA-256) or 9 (scrypt) only when
! supported by the exact target platform and release. Use matching,
! separately provisioned hashes for the local user and enable secret.
! Replace placeholders securely; never store operational hashes here.
! Review existing AAA and retain out-of-band recovery before changes.
! Confirm that only authorized users can access the console, VTYs,
! persistent log files, and other enabled management paths.
!
! Apply from a verified console session: remote management is disabled.
! RESTCONF and NETCONF remain supported product capabilities, but are
! unnecessary in this console-only baseline. Enabling either requires
! a separately approved remote-management policy and secure configuration.
no restconf
no netconf-yang
! Disable legacy NETCONF-over-SSH as well, where supported.
no netconf ssh
no ip http server
no ip http secure-server
!
username <LOCAL-ADMIN> secret <SECRET-TYPE> <PROVISIONED-USER-HASH>
username <LOCAL-ADMIN> privilege 15
enable secret <SECRET-TYPE> <PROVISIONED-ENABLE-HASH>
!
aaa new-model
aaa authentication login default local
aaa authorization exec default local
!
line console 0
 login authentication default
!
! Replace <LAST-VTY> with the highest enabled VTY line.
! Cover every VTY range; deny new SSH, Telnet and other VTY connections.
line vty 0 <LAST-VTY>
 login authentication default
 transport input none
!
! This template does not remove other accounts or disable every service.
! Check for existing sessions separately; do not assume they are terminated.
! Verify console access and rejected remote connections on the target device.
